@description ReaWebAPI: JavaScript Runtime for REAPER
@version 0.3.2
@author zaibuyidao
@link https://github.com/zaibuyidao/ReaWebAPI
@provides
  [win64 extension] reaper_reawebapi-x64.dll https://raw.githubusercontent.com/zaibuyidao/ReaScripts/$commit/ReaWebAPI/extension/reaper_reawebapi-x64.dll
  [darwin-arm64 extension] reaper_reawebapi-arm64.dylib https://raw.githubusercontent.com/zaibuyidao/ReaScripts/$commit/ReaWebAPI/extension/reaper_reawebapi-arm64.dylib
  [darwin64 extension] reaper_reawebapi-x86_64.dylib https://raw.githubusercontent.com/zaibuyidao/ReaScripts/$commit/ReaWebAPI/extension/reaper_reawebapi-x86_64.dylib
  [linux64 extension] reaper_reawebapi-x86_64.so https://raw.githubusercontent.com/zaibuyidao/ReaScripts/$commit/ReaWebAPI/extension/reaper_reawebapi-x86_64.so
  [linux64 extension] reawebapi-webview-x86_64 https://raw.githubusercontent.com/zaibuyidao/ReaScripts/$commit/ReaWebAPI/extension/reawebapi-webview-x86_64
  [linux-aarch64 extension] reaper_reawebapi-aarch64.so https://raw.githubusercontent.com/zaibuyidao/ReaScripts/$commit/ReaWebAPI/extension/reaper_reawebapi-aarch64.so
  [linux-aarch64 extension] reawebapi-webview-aarch64 https://raw.githubusercontent.com/zaibuyidao/ReaScripts/$commit/ReaWebAPI/extension/reawebapi-webview-aarch64
  [script main] web/ReaWebAPI_Demo.lua https://raw.githubusercontent.com/zaibuyidao/ReaScripts/$commit/ReaWebAPI/web/ReaWebAPI_Demo.lua
  [script nomain] web/app.js https://raw.githubusercontent.com/zaibuyidao/ReaScripts/$commit/ReaWebAPI/web/app.js
  [script nomain] web/index.html https://raw.githubusercontent.com/zaibuyidao/ReaScripts/$commit/ReaWebAPI/web/index.html
  [script nomain] web/logo.svg https://raw.githubusercontent.com/zaibuyidao/ReaScripts/$commit/ReaWebAPI/web/logo.svg
  [script nomain] web/style.css https://raw.githubusercontent.com/zaibuyidao/ReaScripts/$commit/ReaWebAPI/web/style.css
@changelog
  Add native macOS WKWebView Web Inspector with right-hand Embedded and native Floating modes, without an additional window frame.
  Add state-aware Open/Hide/Float/Embed context-menu actions and Option+Command+I. Reuse the existing Runtime API and saved layout preferences, retaining the Inspector session across hiding and mode switches.
  Detect WebKit Inspector capabilities at runtime and report native floating fallback when embedding is unavailable.
